      {
        "id": 265024,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-02-03T03:39:55.411Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"73\" data-topic=\"29635\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That being said, I have recently begun my first actual honest-to-goodness long-form, not one-shot/limited series <em><strong>SCRPG</strong></em> game, so there’s some chance that I may post some of the things I make for that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Late to the party, aren’t you?  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">  Best of luck, hope it goes well for you.</p>\n<p>My morale shattered a while ago and I’m not even making token efforts to game any more.  The real world presses in like a vice these days.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"73\" data-topic=\"29635\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hey, I just read <em>All-Star Superman</em> for the first time recently! (Funny when you learn of something and then it feels like it’s everywhere.) It liked it; maybe I should read <em>All-Star Batman &amp; Robin the Boy Wonder</em> next…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>IIRC Solaris was actually introduced in the old 90s DC One Million event (which I rather liked, despite a general distaste for that sort of huge company-wide story), and I don’t think it’s shown up much outside of there.  All-Star Superman (which I absolutely love) is the only one I can think of offhand, but there’s probably some I’ve missed.</p>\n<p>I would recommend some caution about reading All-Star Batman.  It was written by Frank Miller well into his decline into becoming a big bundle of hatred, and has been pretty steadily panned since it came out.  His version of Batman is unpleasant, to put it mildly.  If you go in expecting the kind of celebratory homage to the character’s history that was at the heart of All-Star Superman, it’s going to be like biting into a chocolate candy and having a pair of stainless steel bolts spring out and plunge straight through your cheeks.  I strongly suspect that the poor reception of Miller’s work was in  part responsible for all future “All-Star” projects being dropped and the entire imprint being terminated.</p>\n<p>But hey, at least we got All-Star Superman out of it.</p>",
