      {
        "id": 265033,
        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-02-04T03:36:33.950Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chief_Lackey_Rich\" data-post=\"74\" data-topic=\"29635\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chief_Lackey_Rich:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Late to the party, aren’t you? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Best of luck, hope it goes well for you.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks! And yeah, I got the game several years after it came out, and then I sat on it 'cause I had my plate full DMing <em>D&amp;D</em>.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chief_Lackey_Rich\" data-post=\"74\" data-topic=\"29635\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chief_Lackey_Rich:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>IIRC Solaris was actually introduced in the old 90s DC One Million event (which I rather liked, despite a general distaste for that sort of huge company-wide story), and I don’t think it’s shown up much outside of there. All-Star Superman (which I absolutely love) is the only one I can think of offhand, but there’s probably some I’ve missed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, I’ve not read DC One Million,* though I’ve heard that <em>All-Star Superman</em> and it have a good deal of cross-pollination, due to both having been written by Morrison.</p>\n<p>And yes, I was already aware of <em>All-Star Batman</em>’s infamous reputation; my prior mention of it was pretty much just a joke, hence the ellipsis. : )</p>\n<hr>\n<p>*Though I think I did read the 2007 <em>Booster Gold</em> series’ tie-in to the event, though I’ve no idea why that exists given the rest of the event was apparently in the '90s. Time travel, I guess.</p>",
